      "id": "claim_65c53cd16458419186ef8d5e63188d06",
      "statement": "In the smoke phase, `tools/hx-doc/hx-proof --ready <id>` gates whether a proof step may run: READY means go; NOT READY lists the steps that must close first; NOT RUNNABLE means an implementation decision is still open (NOT_EXECUTABLE). hx-smoke-promote enforces the same chain at promotion, refusing a PASS when a required prior step has not passed and been cited.",
